{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"**No.** Historical exchange volume measures past secondary-market trading—not the liquidity available for your order.\n\nAuthorized participants can deliver a prescribed securities basket and/or cash to the fund in exchange for large blocks of new ETF shares (“creation units”); redemption reverses this process. Market makers can use this mechanism and hedge in underlying markets, linking ETF liquidity to its holdings—not just past ETF turnover.\n\nExamine:\n- **Current bid–ask spreads and displayed depth**, relative to your order size; quotes can change.\n- **Underlying-basket liquidity:** spreads, depth, trading activity, market hours and halts.\n- **Recent trade sizes and price impact**, including during volatility.\n- **Premiums/discounts to NAV**, recognizing that NAV or indicative values can be stale, especially when underlying markets are closed.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Low volume need not mean poor liquidity; high volume does not guarantee a particular order’s execution, size or price."}}
